  "id": "Compound::DB00829 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Diazepam is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c8 through multiple pathways, primarily via its interaction with arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity. The evidence suggests that Diazepam binds to Cyp2c18 or Cyp2b6, which in turn participates in the same enzymatic activity as Cyp2c8. This indicates a potential functional link between Diazepam and Cyp2c8, where the drug may influence the activity of the cytochrome P450 enzyme Cyp2c8 through a shared metabolic pathway. The presence of a common ancestor in the pathway—Benzodiazepine—suggests that Diazepam and its metabolites may share a common mechanism of action, further supporting the notion that Cyp2c8 is a target of Diazepam through this metabolic route. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Diazepam in modulating Cyp2c8 activity, potentially through the activation of arachidonic acid metabolism.",
